  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-06-17T00:37:45.487Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Because it seems that https://feedback.vrchat.com/vrchat-udon-closed-alpha-feedback/p/expose-unique-user-ids-to-udon (May 2020, pretty much no statement from devs) will never be approved for the reason that UserIds are a \"private\" information I think a good idea would be adding Udon only UUID that uniquely identifies a person.\nOf course needs to be accessible through Udon and website publicly by anyone (Don't think there is a need for it to be accessible in game, though can be added to world Tab when that UI update is out)\nThere is a very large and growing amount of creators that are giving special powers to users be it a patreon, moderator, discord member, friend or anything else. And displayName is not a reliable and/or good way for that because of following reasons\n1. there are problems with unicode characters \n2. dots in names are replaced by U+2024 for unknown reason and that can cause issues. \n3. Player changing their names is annoying\n\nIdea originally by @TheHelpfulHelper",
